pe {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c543b2c9-9bd9-5400-aeed-00be99158407" :question/math-academy-id "q-348652" :question/problem "What is the value of $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{t+8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=\\pi ?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(\\pi )=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\pi $ into our function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(\\pi ) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi +8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi +1) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi +8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi +1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26571ec1-e645-5f07-ba4e-75c22558394a" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb99fbc0-cac6-5d79-8483-1e314a68a64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362144} {:answer/id #uuid "acad7e81-2df5-5191-a997-b46b35c6c207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb99fbc0-cac6-5d79-8483-1e314a68a64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362144} :answer-field/id #uuid "a49a9290-7812-55be-9a88-6eed227a2e12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c064f4-ed8a-56b0-a62b-165483d1480c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12c064f4-ed8a-56b0-a62b-165483d1480c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362147} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d603179-2bdd-54fd-b8e7-1de4248c99c7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bac1140e-d9a5-5d46-aa6c-3b47b5403516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac1140e-d9a5-5d46-aa6c-3b47b5403516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362149} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a036ed-a644-5fd3-b0fc-7a95343931ad" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b9301db-160c-5e70-8b92-b15412aa99a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-348653" :question/problem "What is the value of $h(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{3}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=0?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(0)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t=0$ into our function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{3}^{0} \\\\ {0}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "734c3ee4-c63b-5b2d-9d50-556990311461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296804} {:answer/id #uuid "d14f86ac-dcff-55d2-b3b7-af471d436804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "734c3ee4-c63b-5b2d-9d50-556990311461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296804} :answer-field/id #uuid "278e6af9-b46e-5157-8bf0-7abeb45e27e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae45ac93-c493-5bb4-93c6-95e53a04e9aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-348690" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{3}-4},\\,ln\\,(2\\,{e}^{t-2}-1)⟩,$ what is $|r(2)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(2)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨cos\\,(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}),\\,\\sqrt{{2}^{3}-4},\\,ln\\,(2\\,{e}^{0}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,\\sqrt{4},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(2)| & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
